group: C2v
formula: H2O
construction: a central atom and its neighbours
headline: 
note: Fragments: a central atom and its neighbours · energies in Hartree · simplified (Show all levels draws everything) · labels in C<sub>2v</sub> · 1 core orbital hidden
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it. A shell with a non-bonding orbital (one that is at least 99 % that shell, of the orbitals drawn) is drawn at that orbital's energy instead.\n\n**Simplified.** Lines to non-bonding levels are not drawn. Tick Show all levels to draw everything.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in C2v (cross-checked against the code's own CS labels, which agreed on all 25 orbitals both sides could label, and every computed label subduces to match). The structure was symmetrised to C2v for this diagram (atoms moved by up to 0.001 Angstrom); the orbitals are the calculation's own.\n\n**The circles beside each symmetry orbital** show the atoms as seen from one side, filled and open for opposite sign and sized by weight; a bar is a p lobe in the page.\n\n**Not shown.** 1 core orbital below −20.55 Hartree.
